### Interactions

**Forward Flow (Successful Enrollment)**:

```text
Client → API Gateway: POST /enrollments {"firstName": "John", "planId": "GOLD"}

API Gateway → Saga Orchestrator: createEnrollmentSaga(request)

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: INSERT saga (id=SG001, type=ENROLLMENT, state=STARTED, step=0)

Orchestrator → Member Service: POST /members {"firstName": "John"} [Request-ID: SG001-1]
Member Service → Members DB: INSERT member (id=M12345, firstName=John)
Member Service → Orchestrator: 201 Created {"memberId": "M12345"}

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=STEP1_COMPLETE, step=1, memberId=M12345)

Orchestrator → Eligibility Service: POST /eligibility {"memberId": "M12345", "planId": "GOLD"} [Request-ID: SG001-2]
Eligibility Service → Eligibility DB: INSERT eligibility (id=E67890, memberId=M12345, planId=GOLD, effective=2025-01-01)
Eligibility Service → Orchestrator: 201 Created {"eligibilityId": "E67890"}

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=STEP2_COMPLETE, step=2, eligibilityId=E67890)

Orchestrator → Benefits Service: POST /benefits {"memberId": "M12345", "packageId": "GOLD_PLUS"} [Request-ID: SG001-3]
Benefits Service → Benefits DB: INSERT benefits (memberId=M12345, packageId=GOLD_PLUS, deductible=1000)
Benefits Service → Orchestrator: 201 Created {"benefitsId": "B11111"}

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=STEP3_COMPLETE, step=3, benefitsId=B11111)

Orchestrator → Provider Service: POST /pcp/assign {"memberId": "M12345", "pcpNpi": "1234567890"} [Request-ID: SG001-4]
Provider Service → Providers DB: INSERT pcp_assignment (memberId=M12345, pcpNpi=1234567890)
Provider Service → Orchestrator: 201 Created {"pcpId": "P22222"}

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=STEP4_COMPLETE, step=4, pcpId=P22222)

Orchestrator → Notification Service: POST /notifications {"memberId": "M12345", "type": "WELCOME"} [Request-ID: SG001-5]
Notification Service → Orchestrator: 202 Accepted (asynchronous, no compensation needed)

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=COMPLETED, step=5, completedAt=2025-12-26T10:30:00Z)

Orchestrator → API Gateway: 201 Created {"enrollmentId": "M12345", "status": "COMPLETED"}
API Gateway → Client: 201 Created {"enrollmentId": "M12345"}
```

**Compensating Flow (Failed Enrollment at Step 3)**:

```text
[Steps 1-2 complete successfully as shown above]

Orchestrator → Benefits Service: POST /benefits {"memberId": "M12345"} [Request-ID: SG001-3]
Benefits Service → Benefits DB: INSERT benefits (TIMEOUT after 30 seconds, connection pool exhausted)
Benefits Service → Orchestrator: 504 Gateway Timeout

Orchestrator: Detect failure, begin compensation
Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=COMPENSATING, failedStep=3, error="Benefits Service timeout")

Orchestrator → Eligibility Service: DELETE /eligibility/E67890 [Request-ID: SG001-COMP-2]
Eligibility Service → Eligibility DB: DELETE FROM eligibility WHERE id=E67890
Eligibility Service → Orchestrator: 204 No Content

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, compensatedSteps=[2])

Orchestrator → Member Service: DELETE /members/M12345 [Request-ID: SG001-COMP-1]
Member Service → Members DB: DELETE FROM members WHERE id=M12345
Member Service → Orchestrator: 204 No Content

Orchestrator → Saga State Store: UPDATE saga (id=SG001, state=COMPENSATED, compensatedSteps=[2,1], compensatedAt=2025-12-26T10:31:00Z)

Orchestrator → API Gateway: 500 Internal Server Error {"error": "Enrollment failed at Benefits Service", "sagaId": "SG001", "reason": "timeout"}
API Gateway → Client: 500 Internal Server Error {"error": "Enrollment failed, please retry"}
```

**Error Handling and Retry Logic**:

```java
// Saga Orchestrator pseudocode
public class EnrollmentSagaOrchestrator {

    public void executeSaga(EnrollmentRequest request) {
        SagaInstance saga = createSaga(ENROLLMENT, request);

        try {
            // Step 1: CreateMember with retry
            String memberId = retryWithExponentialBackoff(
                () -> memberService.createMember(request.demographics),
                maxRetries = 3,
                initialDelay = 1000ms
            );
            saga.recordStepComplete(1, memberId);

            // Step 2: ActivateEligibility with retry
            String eligibilityId = retryWithExponentialBackoff(
                () -> eligibilityService.activateEligibility(memberId, request.planId),
                maxRetries = 3,
                initialDelay = 1000ms
            );
            saga.recordStepComplete(2, eligibilityId);

            // Step 3: AssignBenefits with retry
            String benefitsId = retryWithExponentialBackoff(
                () -> benefitsService.assignBenefits(memberId, request.packageId),
                maxRetries = 3,
                initialDelay = 1000ms
            );
            saga.recordStepComplete(3, benefitsId);

            // Steps 4-5 continue...

            saga.markCompleted();

        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Failure detected, trigger compensation
            compensate(saga);
            throw new SagaFailedException(saga.getId(), e);
        }
    }

    private void compensate(SagaInstance saga) {
        saga.markCompensating();

        // Compensate in reverse order
        for (int step = saga.getCurrentStep(); step >= 1; step--) {
            try {
                switch (step) {
                    case 3: // Benefits assigned, compensate
                        benefitsService.deleteBenefits(saga.getMemberId());
                        break;
                    case 2: // Eligibility activated, compensate
                        eligibilityService.deleteEligibility(saga.getEligibilityId());
                        break;
                    case 1: // Member created, compensate
                        memberService.deleteMember(saga.getMemberId());
                        break;
                }
                saga.recordCompensationComplete(step);
            } catch (Exception e) {
                // Compensation failed, log and retry later
                log.error("Compensation failed for saga {} step {}", saga.getId(), step, e);
                saga.markCompensationFailed(step, e.getMessage());
                throw e;
            }
        }

        saga.markCompensated();
    }
}
```

